.\" Man page for cfl
.TH CFL 1 "August 2026" "Version 1.1" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
cfl \- dual-pane terminal file manager (ncurses)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfl
.RI [ directory ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfl
is a terminal file manager written in C using the ncurses library. It provides
a dual-pane interface: the left pane lists the current directory, the right
pane shows previews (directory listing, text, hex, or images via Überzugpp)
or file metadata when file-info mode is active.

Features include multi-select, copy/move/delete, FreeDesktop trash, fuzzy
search, bulk delete-search, jump/move/copy destination pickers, bookmarks,
and optional shell integration to
.B cd
into the last browsed directory on quit.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fBdirectory\fR
Directory to open on startup. If omitted, the current working directory is used.

.SH KEY BINDINGS

.SS Navigation
.TP
\fBh\fR
Parent directory.
.TP
\fBj\fR / \fBk\fR
Move selection down / up.
.TP
\fBl\fR / \fBEnter\fR
Enter directory or open file.
.TP
\fBg\fR / \fBG\fR
First / last entry in the directory.
.TP
\fBT\fR / \fBM\fR / \fBB\fR
Top / middle / bottom of the current view.
.TP
\fB.\fR
Toggle hidden files.
.TP
\fBu\fR
Reload current directory.

.SS Search and pickers
.TP
\fB/\fR
Fuzzy search in the current directory (left: matches, right: live preview).
Enter jumps to the match; Esc cancels. Matches prefer shorter names when ranked.
.TP
\fBJ\fR
Jump-to mode: scan directories under
.BR /home ,
.BR /etc ,
and
.B /usr
(errors and basenames in
.B JUMP_OMIT_DIRS
omitted). Type to filter; Enter opens the directory; Esc cancels.
Symlinks are not followed. Results prefer shorter paths.
.TP
\fBD\fR
Delete-search mode: filter the current directory, Tab to mark (dark red
background), right panel shows deletion details. Enter permanently deletes
marked items (or the focused item if none marked). A confirmation dialog
lists every path; y confirms. Esc cancels.
.TP
\fBt\fR
Move-to mode: with a non-empty selection, pick a destination directory
(same scan as jump-to) and move the selection there. Current browsing
directory is unchanged.
.TP
\fBC\fR
Copy-to mode: like move-to, but copies instead of moving.

.SS Selection and file operations
.TP
\fBv\fR
Toggle the current entry in the selection list. Selected rows use a dark
gray full-width bar (same width as the cursor).
.TP
\fBV\fR
Select all files in the current directory.
.TP
\fBc\fR
Clear the selection.
.TP
\fBTab\fR
View the selection list.
.TP
\fBe\fR
Edit the selection list in
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
\fBp\fR
Copy (paste) selection into the
.B current
directory.
.TP
\fBm\fR
Move selection into the
.B current
directory.
.TP
\fBr\fR
Rename selected items (opens editor with paths).
.TP
\fBd\fR
Open the remove menu.
.TP
\fBg\fR
(After
.BR d )
Move selection to FreeDesktop Trash (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
\fBd\fR
(After
.BR d )
Permanently delete selection.
.TP
\fBn\fR
Create a directory.

.SS Preview and info
.TP
\fBi\fR
Toggle file-info mode. The right panel shows metadata instead of previews;
Überzug image previews are stopped. Status shows
.BR [INFO] .
Images: resolution and proportion. Videos: resolution, proportion, FPS,
codec, duration, and size (via
.B mediainfo
when available).
.TP
\fBK\fR
Scroll preview pane up.
.TP
\fB[\fR / \fB]\fR
Page up / page down in the preview pane.
.TP
Image previews (Überzugpp) only clear the previous image when the next
image is smaller or not an image; equal or larger images are drawn without
a full clear for faster browsing.

.SS Other
.TP
\fB=\fR / \fB+\fR / \fB\-\fR
Open / add / remove bookmarks.
.TP
\fB!\fR
Open a shell in the current directory.
.TP
\fB?\fR
Show help.
.TP
\fBq\fR
Quit. Writes the last browsed directory to the lastdir file (see
.BR CFL_LASTDIR ).
With
.B /usr/share/cfl/cfl.sh
sourced, the interactive shell then
.B cd
s to that directory.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell for
.BR ! .
Default
.BR /bin/bash .
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor for rename and selection edit. Default
.BR nvim .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Config base (default
.BR $HOME/.config ).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Data base for Trash (default
.BR $HOME/.local/share ).
.TP
.B CFL_LASTDIR
File path written on quit with the last directory. Default
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/lastdir .

.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/bookmarks\fR
Bookmarks as
.BR key:path .
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/clipboard.<pid>\fR
Session-local selection. Not shared across instances; removed on exit and
after consuming file operations.
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/lastdir\fR
Last directory on quit (for shell helper).
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/scripts\fR
Executable external scripts.
.TP
\fB/usr/share/cfl/cfl.sh\fR
Shell function wrapper for
.B cd
on quit (installed with the package).
.TP
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash\fR
FreeDesktop home trash:
.B files/
holds items,
.B info/*.trashinfo
holds original path and deletion date. Not a raw
.B mv
dump folder.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Compile-time options live in
.BR config.h
(keys, opener, hidden files, trash confirm, jump omit list, Überzugpp
settings). Rebuild after editing.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cfl
Open the current directory.
.TP
.B cfl ~/Downloads
Open a specific directory.
.TP
.B source /usr/share/cfl/cfl.sh
Enable quit-into-last-directory, then run
.BR cfl .

